# Avoid Acting on Stale Code

When a question is not about the current branch (or the PR on the current branch) of a repo, pull the latest `master`/`main` of that repo before answering, so reasoning is based on up-to-date code.

- Fetch and update the default branch first (e.g. `git fetch origin` then read from `origin/master`/`origin/main`), without altering the user's checked-out branch.
- If the question is about the current branch or its PR, use the working tree as-is.
- If pulling latest isn't possible (no network, not a clone, etc.), say so and note the answer may reflect stale code.
